 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law and the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to a public listing of certain not-for-profit corporations",
    "basePrintNo": "S1853",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1853-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §190, Exec L; amd §404, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1853\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the executive law and the\nnot-for-profit corporation law, in relation to a public listing of\ncertain not-for-profit corporations\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill requires a public listing of the certificates of\nincorporation that have been approved by the Adjutant General for\npurposes of soliciting funds or other benefits for the armed forces of\nthe United States or of any foreign country.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one and two direct the Adjutant General, together with the\nDepartment of State, to make public the names of the entities that\nhave been approved for the purpose of soliciting funds or obtaining\nother benefits for the armed forces of the United States or of any\nforeign country.\n\nSection three provides that this act shall take effect 120 days after\nbecoming law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCurrent law requires the Adjutant General to sign off on any\nnot-for-profit incorporating for the purposes of soliciting funds or\nother benefits for the armed forces of the United States, a foreign\ncountry, or the auxiliaries of this state or any other. However, there\nis no public listing of the not-for-profits that have been approved by\nthe Adjutant General.\n\nMaking this information publically available will help New Yorkers,\nwho wish to make donations to not-for-profits incorporated for the\npurpose of supporting our armed forces, ensure that they are donating\nto legitimate organizations.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect 120 days after becoming law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
